    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0538" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60C31/159: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Poland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cudahy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-02-15T18:00:00-05:00">February 15, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>11. Your 13, February 10, 6 p.m.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d403-f1"/> Informal
                    discussions have taken place at the initiative of the Polish Embassy between the
                    Embassy and the Department with a view to ascertaining whether there is any
                    basis for entering into negotiations for the conclusion of a trade agreement
                    with Poland. No decision has yet been reached by the Department with regard to
                    the opening of negotiations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
